        "pl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "01f0d2e9-1043-3677-b384-70907c70579d",
                "word": "heliocentryzm",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "pl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3ebb935d-a5c6-301c-ab70-826493c8b206",
                        "entry_id": "01f0d2e9-1043-3677-b384-70907c70579d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "teoria o centralnym położeniu Słońca we wszechświecie"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "11d20244-9aa7-47e6-91ec-ae8686e17ba8",
                                "sense_id": "3ebb935d-a5c6-301c-ab70-826493c8b206",
                                "text": "Był to nie tylko pierwszy bezpośredni i eksperymentalny dowód heliocentryzmu, ale także okazało się po raz pierwszy, jak ogromna odległość dzieli Układ Słoneczny od innych gwiazd."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c0070f5a-a48e-48dc-94c4-e0e7755953dc",
                                "sense_id": "3ebb935d-a5c6-301c-ab70-826493c8b206",
                                "text": "O sprzyjanie heliocentryzmowi oskarżono również kilku władców."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4f252e3f-d538-4f39-beba-d2ed856b0353",
                        "source_entry_id": "01f0d2e9-1043-3677-b384-70907c70579d",
                        "source_sense_id": "3ebb935d-a5c6-301c-ab70-826493c8b206",
                        "target_lang_word": "heliocentrism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "heliocentrism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c25edeaa-dd49-3f36-a96c-41aaf16810a3",
                                        "entry_id": "5d0c13c6-21ba-3f53-96d8-cfc15d6b462d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The theory that the sun is the center of the universe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a3115dd-eb7e-44ad-ba6f-92206614d4e6",
                                                "sense_id": "c25edeaa-dd49-3f36-a96c-41aaf16810a3",
                                                "text": "1923, Felix Adler, \"The Reconstruction of the Spiritual Ideal,\" American Ethical Union, 68.\nGeocentrism has been displaced by heliocentrism. Heliocentrism, in turn, the claim of the sun, surrounded by its satellites, to a sovereign place in the heavens, has become ridiculous in the face of the wilderness of suns that people the abysses beyond us."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "270b5a5e-a2c2-4f37-96ab-976bd5b7e608",
                                                "sense_id": "c25edeaa-dd49-3f36-a96c-41aaf16810a3",
                                                "text": "It wasn't until the Renaissance that scientists such as Nicolaus Copernicus and Galileo Galilei showed proof for heliocentrism, or the idea that the planets moved around the sun."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b975e764-3b38-31c6-b486-a892df47eb7c",
                                        "entry_id": "5d0c13c6-21ba-3f53-96d8-cfc15d6b462d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The phenomenon of the Earth revolving around the Sun."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb7bd505-1f32-41f4-a0c4-00cd19aea889",
                                                "sense_id": "b975e764-3b38-31c6-b486-a892df47eb7c",
                                                "text": "You would think the practitioners of the dismal science of economics would look at their demand curves and the data on incomes and taxes and pronounce a verdict, the way Galileo and Copernicus did when they showed that geocentrism was a fantasy because the Earth revolves around the sun (known as heliocentrism)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9357885-8fa7-41a1-8faf-a6d75d6d4701",
                                                "sense_id": "b975e764-3b38-31c6-b486-a892df47eb7c",
                                                "text": "Heliocentrism is not yet universally known or accepted. In a 1999 poll, 18 of Americans said that the sun revolves around the Earth, while 79 percent said Earth revolves around the sun."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a4ff4a1b-2f9c-48cc-b942-4c4a950c8f19",
                        "source_entry_id": "01f0d2e9-1043-3677-b384-70907c70579d",
                        "source_sense_id": "3ebb935d-a5c6-301c-ab70-826493c8b206",
                        "target_lang_word": "heliocentricism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "heliocentricism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a8bb6484-3334-38cf-8561-6422072695d9",
                                        "entry_id": "ccd15855-e4e8-331e-9b99-6263b063cf91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of heliocentrism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08459d0e-5ce2-4c26-a436-14f47541bda1",
                                                "sense_id": "a8bb6484-3334-38cf-8561-6422072695d9",
                                                "text": "And as to Copernicus, he declared most expressly in his preface that he spoke of Heliocentricism as a pure hypothesis; the imagination of which was useful for the calculation of planetary orbits, but which “need not be true or even probable,” i.e., resting on any solid ground whatever."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2d73358-7c60-4b5a-a263-05cd9fabefe1",
                                                "sense_id": "a8bb6484-3334-38cf-8561-6422072695d9",
                                                "text": "I do not say for example that Heliocentricism is no truer than Geocentricism, but is only a simpler hypothesis."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fb5cb13c-d674-47bc-94ed-50efde3224a9",
                        "source_entry_id": "01f0d2e9-1043-3677-b384-70907c70579d",
                        "source_sense_id": "3ebb935d-a5c6-301c-ab70-826493c8b206",
